[<<cite:UST2>>, Theorem 2.11] Let $L(\lambda)$ be the finite dimensional irreducible module over $U_q$ of highest weight $\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{n})$. Then there exist a basis of $L(\lambda)$ consisting of all standard tableaux $T(L)$ with fixed top row $l_{nj}=\lambda_j-j$. Moreover, the action of the generators of $U_q$ on $L(\lambda)$ is given by the Gelfand-Tsetlin formulae:

\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
q^{\epsilon_{k}}(T(L))&=q^{a_k}T(L),\quad a_k=\sum_{i=1}^{k}l_{k,i}-\sum_{i=1}^{k-1}l_{k-1,i}+k,\ k=1,\ldots,n,\\
e_{k}(T(L))&=-\sum_{j=1}^{k}
\frac{\prod_{i} [l_{k+ 1,i}-l_{k,j}]_q}{\prod_{i\neq j} [l_{k,i}-l_{k,j}]_q}
T(L+\delta^{kj}),\\
f_{k}(T(L))&=\sum_{j=1}^{k}\frac{\prod_{i} [l_{k-1,i}-l_{k,j}]_q}{\prod_{i\neq j} [l_{k,i}-l_{k,j}]_q}T(L-\delta^{kj}).\\
\end{split}
\end{equation}
